{
  "basis": "The chart's visual data, which shows a clear upward-sloping line from 2,000 in 2010 to approximately 3,000 in 2015, directly contradicts the title's claim of a 'shrinking population'. The visual encoding of the axes (population increasing upward, years progressing left-to-right) confirms that the line represents growth. While the title is present, no policy or authority is provided to override the visual data. The public task and visual notes do not supply a workflow rule that maps observed growth to a specific route, making the 'Route to population growth planning' option the only one that can be selected based on the visual evidence, even if the routing policy is not explicitly defined. The other options ('Route to population decline response' and 'Keep on routine population monitoring') are not supported by the visual data, and no workflow rule is available to justify them.",
  "option_label": "Route to population growth planning"
}
